  "update_count": 59,
  "description_snippet": "This vulnerability exists in 64-bit v8 in the String.p.slit CSA code. The allocation size is stored in int64 but improperly casted to smi which causes the allocated space too small and OOB write. It may potentially lead to remote code execution.  \n  \nPOC  \nvar str2 = String.fromCharCode(0x2c);//add"
